$check_image — filter images by a validation prompt

SUMMARY
  Evaluates each image in images[] against the joined prompt (quality check
  instructions). Failed images are queued for removal via the changes array;
  they are not deleted until the runtime applies changes after the step.

SYNTAX
  $check_image

INPUT
  images[] — candidates to validate.
  prompts[] / prompt_text — criteria text (e.g. "return yes if bad hands").

OUTPUT
  Same bundle as input, plus changes[] entries:
    ("image", "del", <link>) for each failed image.

BEHAVIOR
  Current implementation uses a deterministic hash-based stub (~20% fail
  rate) for testing pipelines. A production version would call vision/LLM
  per image. Use with for(@checker){ @fix } to split bad vs good items.

EXAMPLE
  @filtered: @images -> $check_image
  Check finger count…

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes.
